<STATUS>Not_Reviewed</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>Runtime privileges are the platform's. OpenTrack's compose file does not mount the runtime socket and runs the container non-root, cap_drop ALL, no-new-privileges (docker-compose.yml).</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Platform: container runtime RBAC</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
</VULN>
<VULN>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-233068</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-APP-000133</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-233068r960960_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-APP-000133-CTR-000300</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The container platform must limit privileges to the container platform keystore.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The container platform keystore is used to store credentials used to build a trust between the container platform and some external source. This trust relationship is authorized by the organization. If a malicious user were to have access to the container platform keystore, two negative scenarios could develop:

1) Keys not approved could be introduced and 
2) Approved keys deleted, leading to the introduction of container images from sources that were never approved by the organization. 

To thwart this threat, it is important to protect the container platform keystore and give access to only those individuals and roles approved by the organization.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Review the container platform keystore configuration to determine if the level of access to the keystore is controlled through user privileges. 

Attempt to perform keystore operations to determine if the privileges are enforced. 

If the container platform keystore is not limited through user privileges or the user privileges are not enforced, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the container platform to use and enforce user privileges when accessing the container platform keystore.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>False_Positives</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>False_Negatives</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Documentable</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>false</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Mitigations</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Potential_Impact</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Third_Party_Tools</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Mitigation_Control</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Responsibility</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Security_Override_Guidance</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content_Ref</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>M</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Weight</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>10.0</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Class</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Unclass</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Container Platform Security Requirements Guide :: Version 2, Release: 4 Benchmark Date: 28 Oct 2025</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>5239</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>4bb4bb69-ac34-5cad-97bd-692cd86cae08</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-001499</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STATUS>Not_Reviewed</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>Keystore privileges are the platform's. OpenTrack writes its own session.key owner-only (0600, crates/ot-server/src/auth/mod.rs) and hides source secrets from non-admins (docs/security/stig-mapping.md F-2).</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Platform: keystore RBAC</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
</VULN>
<VULN>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Num</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>V-233069</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Severity</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>medium</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Group_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-APP-000133</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_ID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SV-233069r960960_rule</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Ver</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>SRG-APP-000133-CTR-000305</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Rule_Title</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configuration files for the container platform must be protected.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Vuln_Discuss</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>The secure configuration of the container platform must be protected by disallowing changes to be implemented by non-privileged users. Changes to the container platform can introduce security risks or stability issues and undermine change management procedures. Securing configuration files from non-privileged user modification can be enforced using file ownership and permissions.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>IA_Controls</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Check_Content</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Review the container platform to verify that configuration files cannot be modified by non-privileged users. 

If non-privileged users can modify configuration files, this is a finding.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>Fix_Text</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Configure the container platform to only allow configuration modifications by privileged users.</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>False_Positives</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA></ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
