<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Container Platform Security Requirements Guide :: Version 2, Release: 4 Benchmark Date: 28 Oct 2025</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>5239</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>4bb4bb69-ac34-5cad-97bd-692cd86cae08</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-000172</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STATUS>Open</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>OpenTrack audits successful changes (every decision, including sources, security labels, settings, accounts and roles, is copied into the append-only audit table by record_decision in crates/ot-store/src/sqlite.rs), but a request refused by the role check in the API gate (auth::layer in crates/ot-server/src/auth/mod.rs returns 403 via deny()) writes no audit row and no log line, and successful reads are not audited. Reads of security levels (source security labels, classification order in correlation settings) are not audited, nor are refused attempts.</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Audit (and log as audit.record) every 401/403 refusal in auth::layer with actor, path, method and address; audit reads of security-relevant objects (auth settings, users, tokens, source security labels).</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
</VULN>
