<STATUS>Open</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>OpenTrack audits successful changes (every decision, including sources, security labels, settings, accounts and roles, is copied into the append-only audit table by record_decision in crates/ot-store/src/sqlite.rs), but a request refused by the role check in the API gate (auth::layer in crates/ot-server/src/auth/mod.rs returns 403 via deny()) writes no audit row and no log line, and successful reads are not audited. Deleting an account or revoking a token is audited on success (delete_user, revoke_api_token); refused attempts are not.</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Audit (and log as audit.record) every 401/403 refusal in auth::layer with actor, path, method and address; audit reads of security-relevant objects (auth settings, users, tokens, source security labels).</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
