<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Container Platform Security Requirements Guide :: Version 2, Release: 4 Benchmark Date: 28 Oct 2025</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>5239</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>4bb4bb69-ac34-5cad-97bd-692cd86cae08</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-003831</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STATUS>Not_Reviewed</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>OpenTrack prevents modification (triggers refuse UPDATE/DELETE), detects it (SHA-256 chain, /api/v1/audit/verify logs an error when broken) and logs the chain head hourly so truncation is visible off-host (crates/ot-store/src/audit.rs, crates/ot-server/src/auth/maintenance.rs); alerting personnel is done by the site SIEM on those events.</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Site: SIEM alert on chain-verify errors / head discontinuity</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
</VULN>
