<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIGRef</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>Container Platform Security Requirements Guide :: Version 2, Release: 4 Benchmark Date: 28 Oct 2025</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>TargetKey</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>5239</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>STIG_UUID</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>4bb4bb69-ac34-5cad-97bd-692cd86cae08</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STIG_DATA><VULN_ATTRIBUTE>CCI_REF</VULN_ATTRIBUTE><ATTRIBUTE_DATA>CCI-004909</ATTRIBUTE_DATA></STIG_DATA>
<STATUS>Not_Reviewed</STATUS><FINDING_DETAILS>Each OpenTrack TLS link takes its own CA file (OT_TLS_CLIENT_CA, OT_NATS_CA, OT_REDIS_CA, OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_CERTIFICATE, per-feed ca_file); without one it falls back to the image's Debian ca-certificates system roots (system_roots in crates/ot-source/src/tls.rs). The site must set approved (DoD) anchors on every link or replace the image trust store.</FINDING_DETAILS><COMMENTS>Site: approved trust anchors per link / trust store</COMMENTS><SEVERITY_OVERRIDE></SEVERITY_OVERRIDE><SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION></SEVERITY_JUSTIFICATION>
</VULN>
